Constraints can also be defined at the
*object level*.
```
type BlogPost {
property title -> str;
link author -> User;
constraint exclusive on ((.title, .author));
```
```
type BlogPost {
title: str;
author: User;
constraint exclusive on ((.title, .author));
```
Constraints can contain exceptions; these are called
*partial constraints*.
```
type BlogPost {
property title -> str;
property published -> bool;
constraint exclusive on (.title) except (not .published);
```
...
The
`id` property, all links, and all properties with
`exclusive`
constraints are automatically indexed.

